  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. You should select a (not necessarily contiguous) subsequence of AAA and reverse it. In other words, if you select a subsequence Ai1,Ai2,…,AiKA_{i_1}, A_{i_2}, \\ldots, A_{i_K}Ai1​​,Ai2​​,…,AiK​​ (1≤i1&lt;…&lt;iK≤N1 \\le i_1 \\lt \\ldots \\lt i_K \\le N1≤i1​&lt;…&lt;iK​≤N), then for each valid jjj, the iji_jij​-th element of the resulting sequence is equal to the iK+1−ji_{K+1-j}iK+1−j​-th element of the original sequence; all other elements are the same as in the original sequence.\n\nIn the resulting sequence, you want to calculate the maximum sum of a contiguous subsequence (possibly an empty sequence, with sum 000). Find its maximum possible value and a subsequence which you should select in order to obtain this maximum value. If there are multiple solutions, you may find any one of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2,0001 \\le T \\le 2,0001≤T≤2,000",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\le N \\le 10^52≤N≤105",
      "∣Ai∣≤109|A_i| \\le 10^9∣Ai​∣≤109 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1062 \\cdot 10^62⋅106",
      "Example Input`2",
      "5",
      "-4 2 -4 3 -5",
      "3",
      "-3 -2 -1",
      "`Example Output`5",
      "2 2 3",
      "0",
      "0",
      "`"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print two lines.\n\n\nThe first of these lines should contain a single integer ― the maximum possible sum of a contiguous subsequence.\nThe second line should contain an integer KKK followed by a space and KKK space-separated integers i1,i2,…,iKi_1, i_2, \\ldots, i_Ki1​,i2​,…,iK​.",
